//? Title: Extended Euclid: Actual Remainders, Bezout Witnesses and Safe Inverses
//? Subtitle: Signed-input quotient paths, full int64 certificates and checked legacy result ranges
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Find the greatest common divisor of two integers and coefficients that express
it as their integer combination. Those coefficients also identify modular
inverses when the inputs are coprime. We begin with 240 and 46, inspect every
actual quotient/coefficient row, and retain the original 100,000-pair check.
Signed examples, a Fibonacci family and full-width boundary cases separate
mathematical identities from machine-integer range limits. One widened native
C++ kernel serves ordinary results, unsigned-gcd certificates and optional
owned traces; inverse traces capture their actual solve in the same pass.
)

\toc

> Begin with 240 and 46

Dividing 240 by 46 gives quotient five and remainder ten. Applying that
same row operation to coefficients gives 10=1·240−5·46. Continuing produces
remainders 6,4,2,0, and the last nonzero row is
2=−9·240+47·46. The zero row is still part of the actual execution:
0=23·240−120·46. The five quotients are 5,4,1,1,2.

The following program reads the two initial rows and every derived row
from the native trace. It checks s·a+t·b=r with widened arithmetic and
renders the same stored values. The final sign-normalised result is
separate from the raw rows; in this positive example no sign flip occurs.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/euclid_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");const auto t=dm::algorithms::extended_gcd_trace(240,46);const auto& c=t.outcome.certificate;
  std::print("| row | actual quotient | raw remainder | s | t | exact s*a+t*b |\n| ---: | :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  dm::graphics::Diagram g(52,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=2.6;box.height=.85;box.font_size=22;
  g.text({0,1.8},"remainder r",23).text({4,1.8},"coefficient s",23).text({8,1.8},"coefficient t",23);
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<t.rows.size();++i){const auto& r=t.rows[i];const __int128 check=static_cast<__int128>(t.a)*r.s+static_cast<__int128>(t.b)*r.t;if(check!=r.remainder)throw std::runtime_error("actual row identity failed");const auto q=r.divided?dm::algorithms::int128_text(r.quotient):"initial";
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",i,q,dm::algorithms::int128_text(r.remainder),dm::algorithms::int128_text(r.s),dm::algorithms::int128_text(r.t),dm::algorithms::int128_text(check));
    box.fill=i==t.rows.size()-2?dm::graphics::RGB{187,247,208}:i==t.rows.size()-1?dm::graphics::RGB{226,232,240}:dm::graphics::RGB{191,219,254};
    g.text({-4,-1.5*double(i)},"q = "+q,20);const std::vector<__int128> values{r.remainder,r.s,r.t};for(int col=0;col<3;++col)g.node(std::format("{}:{}",i,col),{4.*col,-1.5*double(i)},dm::algorithms::int128_text(values[col]),box);}
  g.text({3,3.4},"Actual rows maintain r = 240s + 46t",27).text({3,-11.2},std::format("{} divisions; {} coefficient updates; {} retained row records",t.outcome.work.divisions,t.outcome.work.coefficient_updates,t.captured_entries),22).save_svg("build/euclid_tiny.svg");
  std::print("\nOriginal result: gcd {}; x {}; y {}; actual divisions {}; rows {}; normalized {}.\n",c.gcd,c.x,c.y,t.outcome.work.divisions,t.captured_entries,t.outcome.work.sign_normalized);
  if(!dm::algorithms::bezout_certificate_valid(t.a,t.b,c))throw std::runtime_error("gcd certificate failed");
}
