> Signed quotients and sign normalisation are separate facts

C++ division truncates toward zero: −240/46 gives quotient −5 and
remainder −10. A floor quotient would be −6 with positive remainder six;
that is a different row path. Both can express the gcd, but this API
preserves the truncating path and its canonical coefficients.

The actual signed remainder can change sign along a path. Its magnitude
still follows the decreasing unsigned Euclidean sequence. A final sign
flip occurs only when the surviving raw gcd is negative, not whenever
any input is negative. The mixed-sign pair (−240,46) and the pair
(−240,−46) illustrate that distinction. Raw trace rows are retained before
normalisation; result coefficients are the sign-normalised certificate.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/euclid_signed.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");auto raw=dm::graphics::RPlot::create(),magnitude=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();int index=0;
  for(const auto& [a,b]:std::vector<std::pair<std::int64_t,std::int64_t>>{{-240,46},{-240,-46}}){const auto t=dm::algorithms::extended_gcd_trace(a,b);const auto& c=t.outcome.certificate;std::vector<double>x,values,absolute;
    std::print("Signed ({},{}): gcd {}; x {}; y {}; final sign normalized {}; actual divisions {}.\n",a,b,c.gcd,c.x,c.y,t.outcome.work.sign_normalized,t.outcome.work.divisions);
    std::print("| actual row | quotient or initial | raw remainder | s | t |\n| ---: | :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for(std::size_t i=0;i<t.rows.size();++i){const auto& r=t.rows[i];if(static_cast<__int128>(a)*r.s+static_cast<__int128>(b)*r.t!=r.remainder)throw std::runtime_error("signed row identity failed");std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",i,r.divided?dm::algorithms::int128_text(r.quotient):"initial",dm::algorithms::int128_text(r.remainder),dm::algorithms::int128_text(r.s),dm::algorithms::int128_text(r.t));x.push_back(i);values.push_back(static_cast<double>(r.remainder));absolute.push_back(std::abs(static_cast<double>(r.remainder)));}std::print("\n");
    const auto colour=index++?dm::graphics::RGB{220,38,38}:dm::graphics::RGB{37,99,235};const auto label=std::format("{},{}",a,b);raw.line(x,values,label,colour).points(x,values,"",colour,4);magnitude.line(x,absolute,label,colour).points(x,absolute,"",colour,4);}
  raw.title("Raw signed rows").x_label("Captured row index").y_label("Actual remainder");magnitude.title("Magnitudes coincide").x_label("Captured row index").y_label("Absolute remainder");dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(raw).add(magnitude).size(1100,530).title("Truncating division preserves identities despite signed remainders").fit_panels().save_svg("build/euclid_signed.svg");
}
