> Full int64 inputs, narrow results and terminal-row overflow

INT64_MIN has magnitude 2^63, which is not representable as a positive
int64. The legacy three-signed-field result therefore throws overflow for
(INT64_MIN,0), (0,INT64_MIN) and (INT64_MIN,INT64_MIN). The new certificate
stores its nonnegative gcd in uint64 and supports all three while retaining
signed canonical coefficients. The certificate checker uses safe unsigned
magnitudes and checked widened product addition, including malformed claims.

Even a final gcd of one can require wider intermediate arithmetic.
INT64_MIN divided by −1 has quotient +2^63. With divisor one, a terminal
zero row has coefficient +2^63 even though the returned coefficient is
small. Signed128-bit working rows avoid both failures, including updates
that are discarded from the legacy result. Strict old-source sanitizer
probes reproduce division, negation and terminal-coefficient overflows.

Calling std::gcd on signed INT64_MIN violates its representable-magnitude
precondition, even if the final gcd would be small. The boundary program
uses the native certificate checker; independent tests use unsigned
magnitudes and Python arbitrary-precision integers. Ordinary int64
multiplication a*x+b*y is also unsafe for general full-width certificates.
Use widened arithmetic for actual bounded rows or the native checker for
arbitrary claimed int64-coefficient certificates.

Optional trace admission checks its initial two records before allocation
and each next record before its division. The default row cap is one million;
zero disables only that optional quota. Exact and one-short limits are
checked below. Ordinary and work-only calls keep no optional history or
quota. Exceptions expose no partial trace; returned rows own their values.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/euclid_limits.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");const auto minimum=std::numeric_limits<std::int64_t>::min(),maximum=std::numeric_limits<std::int64_t>::max();
  std::print("| a | b | unsigned gcd | x | y | legacy fits | valid certificate |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- | :--- |\n");int overflows=0;
  for(const auto& [a,b]:std::vector<std::pair<std::int64_t,std::int64_t>>{{minimum,0},{0,minimum},{minimum,minimum},{minimum,-1},{minimum,1},{minimum,maximum}}){const auto c=dm::algorithms::extended_gcd_certificate(a,b);bool fits=true;try{(void)dm::algorithms::extended_gcd(a,b);}catch(const std::overflow_error&){fits=false;++overflows;}std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",a,b,c.gcd,c.x,c.y,fits,dm::algorithms::bezout_certificate_valid(a,b,c));}
  const auto q=dm::algorithms::extended_gcd_trace(minimum,-1),terminal=dm::algorithms::extended_gcd_trace(minimum,1);const auto wide=dm::algorithms::extended_gcd_certificate(minimum,0);
  std::print("\nWide actual quotient {}; wide actual terminal coefficient {}; legacy gcd overflow rejections {}.\n",dm::algorithms::int128_text(q.rows.back().quotient),dm::algorithms::int128_text(terminal.rows.back().t),overflows);
  bool malformed_safe=!dm::algorithms::bezout_certificate_valid(minimum,minimum,{1,minimum,minimum});int limits=0;try{(void)dm::algorithms::extended_gcd_trace(240,46,6);}catch(const std::length_error&){++limits;}try{(void)dm::algorithms::extended_gcd_trace(0,0,1);}catch(const std::length_error&){++limits;}
  const auto exact=dm::algorithms::extended_gcd_trace(240,46,7),disabled=dm::algorithms::extended_gcd_trace(240,46,0);std::print("Capture exact {}; disabled {}; one-short/base-short rejections {}/2; overflowing malformed-certificate sum rejected safely {}.\n",exact.captured_entries,disabled.captured_entries,limits,malformed_safe);
  int invalid=0;try{(void)dm::algorithms::modular_inverse(3,0);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++invalid;}try{(void)dm::algorithms::modular_inverse(6,9);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++invalid;}
  const auto zero=dm::algorithms::extended_gcd(0,0);std::print("Invalid inverse rejections {}/2; inverse(INT64_MIN,1) {}; actual zero-pair coefficients {},{}.\n",invalid,dm::algorithms::modular_inverse(minimum,1),zero.x,zero.y);if(overflows!=3||limits!=2||invalid!=2||!malformed_safe)throw std::runtime_error("boundary/quotas failed");
  dm::graphics::Diagram g(58,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=5.2;box.height=2.1;box.font_size=21;box.fill={191,219,254};g.node("gcd",{0,0},std::format("Unsigned gcd\n{}\nlegacy field overflows",wide.gcd),box);box.fill={254,215,170};g.node("quotient",{7,0},"Actual quotient\n"+dm::algorithms::int128_text(q.rows.back().quotient)+"\nfrom INT64_MIN / -1",box);box.fill={187,247,208};g.node("terminal",{14,0},"Actual terminal t\n"+dm::algorithms::int128_text(terminal.rows.back().t)+"\nzero-row coefficient",box)
    .text({7,3.3},"Three distinct reasons to distinguish math from int64 storage",25).save_svg("build/euclid_limits.svg");
}
